# Score domain (`src/lib`)

## Module rules

- **Pure TypeScript** — no `vue`, `pinia`, or `@ionic/vue` imports in `src/lib/**`.
- One concern per file (existing examples: `osmd.ts`, `scoreCache.ts`, `musicXmlAnnotations.ts`, `orchestraPlayer.ts`).
- Export typed functions/types; avoid default exports unless the file already uses them.

## Boundaries

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| `src/lib/*` | Parse/render/export, IndexedDB cache, playback math, MusicXML annotation protocol |
| `src/composables/*` | Vue lifecycle, wiring lib + stores + refs |
| `src/views/**` | Ionic UI, gestures, panel layout |

## MusicXML annotations (do not break)

- App-owned directions use id prefix `fls-ann-*`; embedding/export via `musicXmlAnnotations.ts` (`withEmbeddedAnnotations`, `stripAnnotationArtifacts`).
- Do not rename or duplicate annotation id scheme without updating parse/export and tests.

## Imports in lib

- Prefer relative imports within `lib/` or `@/lib/...` from views/composables — never import from `.vue` files into `lib/`.

## When extending HomePage-related behavior

- Add or extend a `src/lib/<domain>.ts` helper first, then call it from composables or `HomePage.vue` — do not grow inline XML/DOM logic in the page.
